.TH SYS_PROC_INFO 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_info \- query process metadata
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_info(pid_t " pid ", sys_procinfo_t *" info ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_info ()
retrieves process metadata for
.IR pid .
If
.I pid
is 0, the calling process is used.
.PP
The returned record type is
.IR sys_procinfo_t .
Current kernel implementation fills a subset of fields (including
`pid`, `ppid`, `pgid`, `sid`, `uid`, `gid`, `state`, `bitness`,
`start_time`, and `name`).
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On failure, a negative error value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ESRCH
The requested process was not found.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I info
is not writable from userspace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_list (2),
.BR sys_proc_count (2),
.BR getpid (2)
